  "findings": [
    "With debug enabled, the observed raw Page wrapper acknowledged all 500 submitted calls at early export and all 1403 by the later header. Pending was 0 at both snapshots, maximum 2/3, no invocation failures, duplicates or missing callbacks. This does not reproduce a growing callback-bearing raw Page backlog in that observed run.",
    "The maximum callback latency later reached 493 ms. Acknowledgements are not native presentation, render completion or a bound on custom-wrapper/native queues.",
    "The first 16 serialized samples total 18700 UTF8 bytes. This is bounded sampling, not total traffic or retained heap. Typed bufferData uploads likewise measure submitted bytes, not retained JS/native/GPU storage or all texture allocations.",
    "After normal UI disabled debugging and Dfalse was observed, normal 1x playback still showed rapid foreground PSS/RSS/Unknown growth with 40 KiB swap during all 7 samples. Disabling debugging is insufficient as the repair.",
    "The debug-enabled process already had substantial swap and prior-trial state; the two runs are not a clean performance or memory A/B comparison. Reported TOTAL PSS must not be described as physical DRAM or JS heap."
  ],
  "decision": "No production repair is adopted. Debug-off, blocking finish and copy changes have not supplied the required continuous-play result. Observe target JS heap ownership at the next available native snapshot boundary; preserve ordinary rendering and all original acceptance obligations.",
